# Local AI-agent tooling — never project source, and never safe to commit.
#
# .claude/settings.local.json is the important one: it is a per-machine permission allowlist
# that accumulates verbatim copies of previously approved shell commands, so any command that
# ever carried a connection string or API key on its command line is now stored in it in
# plaintext. Until now the only thing keeping it out of a commit was a developer's personal
# ~/.config/git/ignore, which protects one machine and does not travel with the repo — a fresh
# clone, a teammate or CI had no protection at all. This makes the guarantee a property of the
# repository instead.
#
# .claude/skills/ and .agents/skills/ are vendored third-party skill bundles (several MB of
# upstream data), local developer tooling rather than anything this app builds or ships.
#
# Nothing here is deleted by this rule — existing local files stay exactly where they are, they
# simply stop being commit candidates. Force-add deliberately (git add -f) if a genuinely
# shared, secret-free project skill is ever introduced.
.claude/
.agents/
